The drake parser trees the four type forms

A value-type slot on the drake surface now parses to a type-form tree: Atomic as a string leaf,
Objective `(A, B)`, Parametric `F(A, B)` with `[T]`, `{T}` and `{K, V}` as the Seq, Set and Map
applications, and Morphic `A -> B`, binary and grouping to the right as Haskell does. The emitter spells
a tree back to the surface and the engine spells it for Scala, each from the same tree; the assembly
validator reads `ActorRef[M]` structurally rather than as text, and the codec gate's inherited parent
parameters take the target spelling they never needed while every type was host text.

The corpus JSON is re-canonicalized from the drake in the same commit — 37 files across src/main, the
mods actors and the scenario, whose gate asserts that its JSON is what parsing its drake produces — with
the three standing exceptions (BodyElement, ActorAspect, format/json/Value). The elided factory type of
a parameterized type is a tree like any other. `mut {T}` stays host text until `mut` moves to the element. One structural test asserts the
three forms and the right grouping, and both renderings; the JSON gate compares a value type by its one
surface spelling so the string and tree eras agree.

